<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<QuickAction xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE
         <QuickAction> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion. See
         LOI__c.Move_to_Under_Review.quickAction-meta.xml for the full rationale behind this set of
         per-hop actions (user decision, 2026-08-26) and for why no <description> element is used.

         THE TERMINAL HOP. LOI_DISPOSITION_NEXT_STAGE maps 'Negotiation' => 'Signed'. 'Signed' is
         terminal on BOTH record types and is deliberately NOT a key in either map - adding a hop
         out of it would move a sale past its own end state.

         🔴 BOTH LITERALS ARE SHARED WITH Acquisition_LOI, SO THE RECORD-TYPE CRITERION IS
         LOAD-BEARING. On the acquisition side 'Negotiation' is reached from 'Submitted' via
         LOI__c.Mark_Countered and is followed by 'Signed' via the ordinary Advance Stage button,
         which additionally tests Is_Advance_Allowed__c. A stage-only rule would render this button
         alongside that one on an acquisition LOI.

         ⚠ THIS BUTTON ALSO CARRIES {!Record.Is_Advance_Allowed__c} EQUAL true, exactly as the
         disposition Advance_Stage entry it replaces did. That formula's only clause this action's
         exact stage test does not already subsume is TEXT(LOI_Status__c) <> "Pending Approval" -
         dropping it would have handed the sell side a way to advance an LOI mid-approval that the
         generic button refused. The clause cannot be written as a criterion directly:
         LOI__c.LOI_Status__c has NO field permission on DPEG_Disposition_Edit or
         DPEG_Disposition_View (measured), and a visibility rule reading a field the running user
         cannot read evaluates FALSE - it would hide the button permanently. A FORMULA field is
         evaluated server-side and has no such dependency. -->
    <actionSubtype>Action</actionSubtype>
    <label>Signed</label>
    <lightningWebComponent>advanceRecordStage</lightningWebComponent>
    <optionsCreateFeedItem>false</optionsCreateFeedItem>
    <type>LightningWebComponent</type>
</QuickAction>
